WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.967
Routing should begin with the information need.

00:00:02.967 --> 00:00:06.442
Do not ask the router which answer sounds likely.

00:00:06.442 --> 00:00:08.942
Ask what evidence is required.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:14.292
If the question is, what is the return deadline, route to policy search.

00:00:14.292 --> 00:00:21.142
If the question is, when was order one zero four two delivered, route to order lookup.

00:00:21.142 --> 00:00:26.984
If the question is, can order one zero four two still be returned, we need both.

00:00:27.696 --> 00:00:30.218
Some requests need no tool.

00:00:30.218 --> 00:00:35.578
If the user simply says thank you, the workflow can answer directly.

00:00:35.578 --> 00:00:40.218
A router also does not always need one exclusive route.

00:00:40.218 --> 00:00:46.004
State can record needs policy equals true and needs order equals true.

00:00:46.627 --> 00:00:50.994
For a project, design routes around evidence requirements.

00:00:50.994 --> 00:00:57.349
That makes the routing decision easier to evaluate because you can label which sources each test question actually

00:00:57.349 --> 00:00:58.998
needs.
